{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And this stone, etc.</b> It would appear that this is the Even Shetiyah (Zohar 1:72) which he prepared for the Sanctuary, and we find that he prepared shittim wood for the Tabernacle in the wilderness (Tanchuma, Terumah). Or perhaps HaShem intends, in saying ״וְעָשׂוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ״ (Exodus 25:8), the language of that which is prepared — meaning, that which had already been prepared beforehand — for the Tabernacle and also the Temple, both of them Jacob prepared; ״וְשָׁכַנְתִּי בְּתוֹכָם״ refers back to these two acts of preparation."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:20.738513569Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}